## 4. Homeserver churn / mortality — measured

**The only live longitudinal dataset I found:** Matrix Rooms Search (MRS) by **etke.cc**, endpoint https://api.matrixrooms.info/stats (site https://matrixrooms.info/). It carries a **59-point timeline from 2024-02-10 to 2026-09-04**. Method: discovery via public room directories, so "online" servers is a **lower bound** on the federation, and the room count is only *indexable* rooms.

Snapshot **2026-09-04**: **20,232 servers online**, 4,137 indexable, 19,980 rooms indexed.
Server software split (2026-09-04): **Synapse 15,713 (77.7%)** · continuwuity 1,806 · tuwunel 1,698 · conduit 539 · dendrite 310 · other 166.

Selected timeline (servers online / indexable / rooms indexed):

| Date | online | indexable | rooms |
|---|---|---|---|
| 2024-02-10 | 8,837 | 2,492 | 20,573 |
| 2024-10-01 | 10,092 | 3,096 | 21,387 |
| 2025-02-01 | 10,496 | 3,112 | 22,211 |
| 2025-07-01 | 13,099 | 3,765 | 18,386 |
| 2025-09-01 | 12,810 | 3,691 | 17,915 |
| **2025-10-01** | **10,726** | 3,066 | 17,963 |
| 2026-01-01 | 12,007 | 3,236 | 17,765 |
| 2026-05-04 | 19,181 | 4,267 | 20,325 |
| 2026-09-04 | 20,232 | 4,137 | 19,980 |

Findings from this series:
- **Server count grew 2.3× in 31 months** (8,837 → 20,232), but the count is not monotone: **−16.3% in one month, 2025-09-01 → 2025-10-01** (12,810 → 10,726). That window straddles the matrix.org 24h outage of 2025-09-02; whether the drop is real churn or crawler blindness during that outage **cannot be settled from this data** — treat it as an instrument-lie candidate, not a churn measurement.
- Synapse's share fell across the series where software is reported: **2025-10-01 Synapse 9,293 / 10,726 = 86.6%** → **2026-09-04 15,713 / 20,232 = 77.7%** (DERIVED). continuwuity went 241 → 1,806 (**7.5×** in 11 months); tuwunel 224 → 1,698.
- **Indexable servers are flat-to-declining while online servers doubled**: 3,691 (2025-09) → 4,137 (2026-09), i.e. the share of servers exposing a public room directory fell from ~29% to **20.4%**.
- **Indexed rooms are flat or shrinking** (20,573 in Feb 2024 → 19,980 now) while servers 2.3×'d.

**Curated public-homeserver supply is tiny.** https://servers.joinmatrix.org/servers.json (fetched 2026-09-04, maintained by Austin Huang, explicitly *not* Foundation-affiliated): **24 public servers + 22 private**, **all 24 running Synapse**; hosting concentrated on **Hetzner (8 of 24)**. The Foundation's own 2024-03 post pointed users at this list as the exit ramp from matrix.org.

**Dead / unreachable trackers (negative findings):**
- **matrixstats.org — NOT REACHED**, DNS/connection failure (curl exit code 000). Appears defunct.
- **the-federation.info — NOT REACHED**, HTTP **502** on two attempts. (It tracks diaspora/Friendica-family anyway.)
- **stats.matrix.org — NOT REACHED** (connection failure).
- No academic longitudinal churn study exists: arXiv `all:"Matrix federation"` = **1 result total** (the 2019 KIT paper). "Matrix protocol: a comprehensive systematic mapping study" (2026, J. Cloud Computing, doi:10.1186/s13677-025-00829-7, PDF fetched, 29 pp.) is a **literature survey with zero measured federation statistics** — no server counts, no user counts, no resource benchmarks; latency/scalability discussed only qualitatively.
- Other OpenAlex hits that look adjacent but are not measurements of the federation: "Uma investigação sobre tolerância a falhas no servidor de comunicação Synapse" (2025, doi:10.5753/wtf.2025.8814), "A Comparative Performance Study of the Matrix /sync Endpoint on Synapse and Tuwunel" (2026, doi:10.5753/sbrc.2026.19722) — **both NOT READ** (Portuguese-language SBC proceedings; landing pages not fetched this session). OpenAlex began rate-limiting mid-session.

---

## The load-bearing figures, compressed

- Foundation FY2025: **£910,821 cost, £310,596 loss, ~£600k revenue**; loss = 34% of cost, improved from 50%.
- **~50% of all Foundation expenditure is attributable to running one homeserver** (20% infra + T&S moderation).
- **One member (Automattic) = 50% of revenue**; Element's Platinum contribution doesn't even appear as revenue.
- Donations were **$6k/mo against Element's $400k/mo** in 2022; Element still contributes **£3M+/yr** in-kind and wrote **>95%** of core code.
- The Foundation has publicly stated the alternative to charging is "**to turn off the server**" (2025-06) and that "**the end of the road is in sight**" (2025-02).
- **~32% of the entire open federation's MAU sits on matrix.org** (370k / 1.15M).
- The one peer-reviewed crawl found **top 1% of servers held 87% of users**, and that the biggest server **sent 88.4% of all inter-server messages** — decentralizing *raises* aggregate load under Matrix's fan-out.
- A hobby homeserver's documented floor is **1GB RAM (Synapse) / 8GB + 2-4 cores (Dendrite)**, with **~92% database waste** demonstrated in the field; matrix.org's ceiling is **51TB of Postgres on bare metal with hundreds of workers**.
- Federation server count is **growing (8.8k → 20.2k in 31 months)** but Synapse's share is **falling (86.6% → 77.7% in 11 months)**, and no public tracker measures per-server mortality.
